# clang-format before commit

CI `lint` uses **clang-format 18** with `--dry-run --Werror` on all `src/`, `include/`, and `tests/` `*.cc` / `*.h` files.

## Before every commit that touches C++

1. Format and verify:
   ```bash
   ./scripts/check-format.sh --fix
   ./scripts/check-format.sh
   ```
2. If local `clang-format` is v14, use Docker (matches CI):
   ```bash
   docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/src" -w /src ubuntu:24.04 bash -c \
     'apt-get update -qq && apt-get install -qq -y clang-format-18 >/dev/null && \
      find src include tests -type f \( -name "*.cc" -o -name "*.h" \) -print0 \
      | xargs -0 clang-format-18 -i'
   ./scripts/check-format.sh
   ```

## Enable the git hook (once per clone)

```bash
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
```

## Style

Follow `.clang-format` (LLVM, column limit 100). Do not hand-wrap lines in ways that v18 re-breaks — run the checker instead.
